Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.84,0:00:06.30,flashback,Regulus,0,0,0,,Look, you must be joking.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.30,0:00:09.72,flashback,Regulus,0,0,0,,Getting all big-headed just \Nbecause you got a tiny bit lucky!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.72,0:00:11.92,flashback,Petelgeuse,0,0,0,,Revolting and despicable!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.92,0:00:16.03,flashback,Petelgeuse,0,0,0,,What a self-righteous piece\Nof work you are!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.03,0:00:20.79,flashback,Regulus,0,0,0,,Really, when will you feel you've had \Nenough of making people look foolish?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.79,0:00:25.04,flashback,Petelgeuse,0,0,0,,Ah, and here I am, so vehemently \Nand diligently appealing to you!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.04,0:00:28.81,flashback,Petelgeuse,0,0,0,,Just how slothful can you be?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.81,0:00:34.32,flashback,Regulus,0,0,0,,You're violating my rights as an \Nunselfish man who desires nothing but
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.32,0:00:37.39,flashback,Regulus,0,0,0,,to settle for a tiny bit of \Nsimple, ordinary happiness!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.81,0:00:58.28,flashback,Witch of Envy,0,0,0,,I love you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.28,0:01:07.50,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I'm... inside the carriage?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.96,0:01:12.15,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Emilia?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.69,0:01:16.05,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I didn't... Return by Death, did I?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.39,0:01:20.85,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,She's so soft and warm.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.38,0:01:24.52,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,Try not to get up to too much mischief.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.52,0:01:25.73,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Howawha?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.73,0:01:29.12,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,Emilia lost two nights of sleep \Nworrying about you, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.12,0:01:32.36,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Oh, thank goodness you're \Nokay! And the others?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.36,0:01:36.40,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,Don't worry. Everyone is \Nsafely together, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.40,0:01:39.62,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Man, what a huge relief! I was so worried!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.62,0:01:41.21,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Let me hug you!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.33,0:01:50.44,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Is this...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.44,0:01:51.44,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,It is.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.97,0:01:56.84,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,The inside of the Pleiades \NWatchtower, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.45,0:02:06.43,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,You're...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.66,0:02:11.94,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Who are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.58,0:02:14.06,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Are you the Sage?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.06,0:02:15.53,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,I finally found you...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.03,0:02:16.99,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Master.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.99,0:02:23.04,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.04,0:02:27.26,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Oh, man! Oh, man! Oh, man! \NI've been waiting {\i1}so long{\i0}!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.26,0:02:29.90,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,Wh-Wh-What is the meaning of this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.90,0:02:32.50,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,It's been forever! I missed you so much!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.00,0:02:31.17,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Hold it! Hold it! Hold it!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.88,0:02:34.59,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.59,0:02:36.17,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,What is this brute strength?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.17,0:02:38.92,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Who even are you, and what is going on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.92,0:02:41.92,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,What do you mean?! I'm Shaula!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.92,0:02:43.83,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Keeper of the Pleiades Watchtower,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.83,0:02:47.52,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,and your precious student, Shaula!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.29,0:02:52.27,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,There's trouble! I woke \Nup and Subaru was go—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.40,0:02:58.06,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Emilia-tan, help me!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.53,0:03:01.66,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,Hiyah!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.66,0:03:03.32,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Wait, why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.32,0:03:07.20,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,I don't know! I just feel {\i1}very{\i0} upset!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.85,0:03:13.17,main,Julius,0,0,0,,Subaru, please try not to let us down.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.04,0:03:16.92,main,Ram,0,0,0,,You're making a lewd face, Pervarusu.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.92,0:03:19.22,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I am not, and don't mash \Nthose words together!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.22,0:03:22.13,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Master! Master!\NI'll never leave you again!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.13,0:03:25.97,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Anyway! I'd like to start discussing \Nthings before my arm gets ripped off!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.97,0:03:28.41,main,Anastasia,0,0,0,,We're just as baffled as you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.41,0:03:33.27,main,Anastasia,0,0,0,,This woman who barely said a word before \Nis hangin' all over Natsuki now.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.08,0:03:35.20,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Her?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.20,0:03:36.65,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,You said it yourself, Master.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.33,0:03:40.36,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,No matter what anyone asks, \Ndon't say more than you need to!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.36,0:03:42.03,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Don't talk! Don't tell!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.03,0:03:43.86,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Hell, just stab 'em dead first!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.86,0:03:46.66,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,I was just doing what you taught me!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.66,0:03:48.79,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Your master was pretty awful, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.68,0:03:52.78,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Forget all that. You can \Ntalk to everybody else, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.79,0:03:57.50,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Oh, man! This is awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.50,0:04:00.34,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Master gave me permission!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.84,0:04:05.20,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Okay, so you {\i1}are{\i0} the Sage we've \Nheard so much about, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.20,0:04:06.47,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Hmm...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.47,0:04:10.06,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,If it's a "Shaula" you're \Nlooking for, yeah, that's me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.34,0:04:12.01,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,I guess my love is mutual!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.01,0:04:14.77,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,But if it's a "Shaula the \NSage" you're looking for,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.77,0:04:16.61,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,I dunno anything about 'em.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.61,0:04:21.11,main,Anastasia,0,0,0,,This is the Shaula that people \Nmean when they say "Shaula."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.57,0:04:25.64,main,Anastasia,0,0,0,,The holy gold coin has the Holy Dragon,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.64,0:04:27.41,main,Anastasia,0,0,0,,the gold has the first Sword Saint,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.41,0:04:28.78,main,Anastasia,0,0,0,,and the silver has the Sage.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.11,0:04:31.89,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,She doesn't look the least \Nbit like this, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.89,0:04:34.42,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Wow, that looks just like Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.81,0:04:36.41,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Me?! How?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.41,0:04:40.38,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,I don't think this person really \Nlooks like Subaru, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.38,0:04:46.26,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Oh, I didn't recognize Master \Nbased on his looks, so no problem!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.26,0:04:48.51,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Where exactly did you learn that phrase?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.51,0:04:51.76,main,Julius,0,0,0,,If it wasn't his looks, \Nhow did you recognize him?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.76,0:04:53.10,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,His smell!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.10,0:04:57.30,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,The only person who gives\Noff such a nose-burningly black,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.30,0:04:59.69,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,disgusting smell is Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.69,0:05:02.58,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I've never felt so hurt before in my life!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.58,0:05:04.88,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Seriously? Do I smell that bad?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.88,0:05:07.00,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,D-Don't worry, Subaru.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.00,0:05:11.08,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,I understand. Let's make sure \Nwe have proper baths later.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.08,0:05:13.08,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,You don't understand at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.24,0:05:17.04,main,Ram,0,0,0,,So you are Shaula,\Nbut you aren't the Sage.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.60,0:05:20.29,main,Ram,0,0,0,,Then do the Sword Saint and Holy \NDragon sound familiar to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.29,0:05:21.93,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Blech!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.93,0:05:23.01,main,Ram,0,0,0,,I guess so.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.01,0:05:25.09,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Of course I've heard of them!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.09,0:05:28.92,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,I've known Reid the stick swinger \Nand Volcanica the sarcastic forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.92,0:05:31.02,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,They're probably doing pretty \Ngood these days, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.02,0:05:33.30,main,Ram,0,0,0,,Reid has been dead for years.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.30,0:05:34.63,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,For real?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.63,0:05:37.87,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,He seemed like a guy nobody \Ncould kill! How'd he die?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.87,0:05:39.01,main,Ram,0,0,0,,Old age.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.01,0:05:42.86,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah.\NI guess he was a human, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.86,0:05:46.74,main,Ram,0,0,0,,I'll ask you straight. \NJust who is your master?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.47,0:05:49.36,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,That's a weird question.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.36,0:05:51.49,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,You guys are traveling with \Nhim. Shouldn't you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.90,0:05:57.18,main,Ram,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, but your master hit his head \Non a chamber pot and forgot many things.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.18,0:05:59.40,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Really, Master? {\i1}Again?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.40,0:06:00.32,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,"Again"?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.32,0:06:03.59,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,All right, then, I'll make \Nthe big announcement.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.59,0:06:08.05,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,My master's name—yes, the name \Nof the great, renowned wise man!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.44,0:06:13.51,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,The only one in this world worthy \Nof being known as the Sage!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.56,0:06:16.73,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,We don't need a drumroll.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.73,0:06:18.44,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Tah-da!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.13,0:06:20.10,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Flügel!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.28,0:06:24.07,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.53,0:06:27.65,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,My master's name is Flügel.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.32,0:06:30.61,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Flügel the Wise Man!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.56,0:06:41.11,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Isn't that the name of the \Nguy who planted that tree?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.00,0:06:48.47,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Damn, that's scary! We're so high up!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.47,0:06:51.02,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,And not even a handrail to \Noffer a sense of security!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.02,0:06:55.56,main,Meili,0,0,0,,Hey, naked lady,\Nthis ride is way too bouncy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.56,0:06:59.31,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,A kid getting a free ride \Nshouldn't be so demanding.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.87,0:07:02.32,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Hey! Quit pulling my hair!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.32,0:07:05.26,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Come on, Meili. Don't antagonize her.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.26,0:07:06.98,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,And no playing with her ponytail.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.98,0:07:10.34,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,It's not a ponytail. It's a scorpion tail.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.34,0:07:10.95,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.82,0:07:13.57,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Scorpion tail!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.00,0:07:17.75,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Okay, fine. Why get so hung up on {\i1}that{\i0}?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.89,0:07:23.50,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,This door serves as the tower's \Nprimary entrance and exit, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.50,0:07:26.73,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,Rem and Patrasche are\Non the next floor up.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.73,0:07:28.06,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,We have to go higher?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.06,0:07:32.72,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Also, if {\i1}this{\i0} is the entrance, how did \NPatrasche and the carriage get that far?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.04,0:07:35.62,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,Shaula carried everything for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.62,0:07:37.46,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,She just went, "Hup!" And lifted them up.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.13,0:07:38.93,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Pardon?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.93,0:07:40.71,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Aw, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.71,0:07:43.19,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,That was a piece of cake!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.19,0:07:46.19,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I'm more freaked out than grateful.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.19,0:07:48.55,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Whether you're grateful or freaked out,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.55,0:07:52.72,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,please just accept my \Nearnest feelings for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.72,0:07:53.60,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Smack.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.60,0:07:55.16,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,You threw 'em away?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.97,0:08:02.22,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,So I guess Flügel built all this, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.22,0:08:05.44,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,You know,\NI heard he was known as the Sage,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.44,0:08:08.16,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,but I never thought I'd \Nhear about him again here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.16,0:08:12.30,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,I don't really know what he did other \Nthan planting that tree, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.30,0:08:14.33,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,This tower sure is huge, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.33,0:08:16.41,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,It's finally starting to hit me now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.41,0:08:17.85,main,Julius,0,0,0,,What's starting to hit you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.85,0:08:21.77,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,That this is the Pleiades Watchtower \Nthat we were trying to reach.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.77,0:08:23.35,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Tsk, tsk, tsk.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.35,0:08:27.52,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,If that's all you understand,\Nyou get a 99 out of 100 at best.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.52,0:08:29.02,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,That's basically a perfect score!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.02,0:08:32.56,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Well, that score factors in bonus points
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.56,0:08:35.74,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,for how much I love, love, {\i1}love{\i0} you!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.43,0:08:41.09,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Pleiades Watchtower is just a \Ntemporary name for a temporary role.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.09,0:08:45.81,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Now that you've returned,\Nit'll go back to its original role.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.81,0:08:47.43,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Its original role?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.43,0:08:48.21,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Yep!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.50,0:08:54.09,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,A great library where you can find \Neverything you ever wanted to know!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.18,0:09:01.73,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,The Great Pleiades Library is so, \Nso, so, {\i}so{\i0} happy to have you back!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.09,0:09:06.52,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Rem and Patrasche are in here?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.91,0:09:10.36,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Whoa! Ram, the vines moved!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.36,0:09:11.95,main,Ram,0,0,0,,You're too jumpy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.95,0:09:13.82,main,Ram,0,0,0,,You'll startle the room's master.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.82,0:09:16.49,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,The room's... master?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.07,0:09:18.14,main,Ram,0,0,0,,A spirit.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.07,0:09:29.59,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,It feels like a jungle.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.77,0:09:41.97,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Rem...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.97,0:09:43.42,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,And Patrasche.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.04,0:09:45.93,main,Ram,0,0,0,,When we rejoined Lady Emilia,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.30,0:09:48.97,main,Ram,0,0,0,,Patrasche was gravely injured.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.97,0:09:51.59,main,Ram,0,0,0,,The spirit's power has been healing her.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.85,0:09:55.61,main,Ram,0,0,0,,The spirit living here doesn't \Nseem to have anything like a will.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.41,0:10:00.57,main,Ram,0,0,0,,It only tries to heal the illnesses \Nand injuries of creatures who enter.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.57,0:10:02.30,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Then could it heal Rem?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.34,0:10:05.36,main,Ram,0,0,0,,It doesn't work on Rem.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.36,0:10:07.99,main,Ram,0,0,0,,It can't heal something that \Nisn't an illness or injury.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.99,0:10:10.00,main,Ram,0,0,0,,That's what the spirit decided.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.31,0:10:15.09,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,So in other words, after \Nall this, nothing changes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.09,0:10:18.76,main,Ram,0,0,0,,If you want to change it, you must\Nachieve the objective of your tower visit.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.41,0:10:22.72,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,The Great Pleiades Library, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.93,0:10:28.06,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I'll find the answer and get Rem back.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.06,0:10:30.60,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,That goal hasn't changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.60,0:10:34.61,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Okay! I'm going back to the others. You?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.61,0:10:39.32,main,Ram,0,0,0,,Aren't you too worried to leave \NRem with no one watching her?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.97,0:10:42.53,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Okay, then,\NI'll leave you in charge of her.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.02,0:10:45.34,main,Ram,0,0,0,,Although all I can do is watch over her...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.87,0:10:50.03,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,You watching over her means plenty.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.04,0:11:04.22,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Please take care of Rem and Patrasche.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.72,0:11:10.85,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,This floor is basically my den.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.85,0:11:13.71,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,I spend most of my time \Nwatching the dunes from here,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.71,0:11:17.60,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,and anyone who gets close to \Nthe tower gets shot! Shot!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.60,0:11:19.19,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I knew it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.19,0:11:20.78,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,That was you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.78,0:11:23.62,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,You have no idea what I went \Nthrough because of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.62,0:11:27.02,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,A shot that keeps interfering \Npests away from the tower:
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.02,0:11:28.84,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Hell's Snipe!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.58,0:11:31.52,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,Was everything all right inside?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.52,0:11:34.29,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Yeah, they're fine. Ram's watching them.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.96,0:11:41.18,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,We don't know what she'll do if \Nshe finds out you're not Flügel.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.18,0:11:43.98,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,So we can't correct her\Nor let her know, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.98,0:11:46.88,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Regulus and Petelgeuse were so much \Neasier to deal with than this.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.88,0:11:49.44,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Master! Somethin' wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.44,0:11:51.39,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Not a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.39,0:11:54.31,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I just want to make sure of one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.31,0:11:57.24,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,The reason you shot people \Napproaching the tower was...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.24,0:12:00.32,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Your orders, of course, Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.32,0:12:05.16,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,For 400 years, I spent every single \Nday watching that sea of sand.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.16,0:12:09.66,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,It's a story so sad, both hearing it \Nand telling it make me want to cry!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.29,0:12:12.91,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,You were all alone for 400 years?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.01,0:12:17.56,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,You'll do anything I tell you, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.56,0:12:20.55,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Wh-What's that serious expression for?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.55,0:12:22.69,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,I won't do anything perverted.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.69,0:12:25.59,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Don't harm me or my friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.55,0:12:32.46,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Your master's orders were to attack \Nanyone approaching the tower, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.46,0:12:36.48,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,So now that we're inside it, \Nthere's no need to attack us.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.48,0:12:38.98,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Do not harm us. No matter what.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.69,0:12:43.54,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Okay, got it!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.54,0:12:48.01,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,I've committed it to my memory as \Nmy new orders from you, Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.01,0:12:50.15,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Good. That's a promise, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.15,0:12:51.89,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Roger that!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.89,0:12:55.12,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,I'll protect you all! I'll \Nprotect the hell out of ya!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.70,0:13:00.67,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Once again, welcome back, Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.00,0:13:07.80,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,I, Shaula, have waited most eagerly for \Nthe return of Flügel the Wise Man!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.76,0:13:15.48,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,We've come as high as the sixth, \Nfifth, and fourth floors.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.82,0:13:19.94,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Above here is the exam site that takes \Nup the third, second, and first floors.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.94,0:13:21.33,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Exam site?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.33,0:13:23.50,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Yep. On the third floor,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.50,0:13:26.37,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,you'll be tested to make sure you \Nqualify to enter the archive.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.37,0:13:29.66,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,You have to qualify to enter the \NGreat Pleiades Library's archive?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.66,0:13:33.68,main,Julius,0,0,0,,That is the greatest challenge \Nwe face at present.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.68,0:13:39.01,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I see. So the rest of you took \Nthat exam while I was asleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.36,0:13:49.97,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,This looks like a room I wouldn't \Nwant to stay in very long.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.97,0:13:51.05,main,Julius,0,0,0,,I agree.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.45,0:13:54.27,main,Julius,0,0,0,,Staying long in here would rob \Nyou of your sense of equilibrium.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.27,0:14:05.40,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,A stone... slab?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.40,0:14:10.38,main,Julius,0,0,0,,One might call it the device \Nthat sets up the puzzle for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.38,0:14:14.37,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,When you touch that slab,\Nthe exam will begin, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.62,0:14:17.83,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I just need to touch this monolith?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.40,0:14:22.31,main,Julius,0,0,0,,Monolith? Somehow, that \Nname seems rather fitting.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.31,0:14:23.42,main,Julius,0,0,0,,I'll use that henceforth.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.93,0:14:24.88,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Here I go.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.27,0:14:46.65,main,Voice,0,0,0,,Hero vanquished by Shaula,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.31,0:14:50.29,main,Voice,0,0,0,,touch upon his grandest splendor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.14,0:14:52.30,main,Julius,0,0,0,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.36,0:14:57.97,main,Julius,0,0,0,,Do you see now why we were \Nso surprised at first?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.75,0:15:05.07,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,So what I just heard was an exam question?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.07,0:15:08.92,main,Julius,0,0,0,,Subaru, there are a few things you \Nmust know before beginning the exam.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.92,0:15:14.64,main,Julius,0,0,0,,First, try touching the slab—rather, \Nthe monolith closest to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.64,0:15:16.55,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,You like the word that much?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.55,0:15:18.39,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I mean, that's fine, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.23,0:15:27.11,main,Julius,0,0,0,,You've returned to the starting point.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.66,0:15:31.11,main,Julius,0,0,0,,In other words, it was determined \Nthat you failed the exam.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.40,0:15:32.32,main,Julius,0,0,0,,Naturally...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.88,0:15:41.71,main,Voice,0,0,0,,Hero vanquished by Shaula,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.71,0:15:44.75,main,Voice,0,0,0,,touch upon his grandest splendor.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.36,0:15:49.72,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I see. So I can keep trying \Nover and over until I pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.72,0:15:52.72,main,Julius,0,0,0,,That is our conjecture at present.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.00,0:15:57.97,main,Julius,0,0,0,,Just running around touching monoliths\Nblindly will not lead you to the answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.97,0:15:59.68,main,Julius,0,0,0,,That is all I can tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.68,0:16:02.63,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,So you guys already tried the \Nscattershot approach, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.45,0:16:07.53,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,That does seem like something \Nyou'd try, Emilia-tan.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.53,0:16:10.98,main,Anastasia,0,0,0,,Still, even if you know the answer,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.98,0:16:15.12,main,Anastasia,0,0,0,,what do you have to do to "touch \Nupon his greatest splendor"?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.88,0:16:17.42,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,True...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.42,0:16:21.01,main,Meili,0,0,0,,Well, you won't get anywhere standing \Nhere thinking about it forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.01,0:16:24.57,main,Meili,0,0,0,,I think you should try \Nasking the naked lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.57,0:16:26.33,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I guess so.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.61,0:16:30.47,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Shaula! Can you think of any heroes \Nyou've vanquished who fit the bill?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.47,0:16:35.12,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Only second-rates remember the \Nnames of all the people they kill!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.12,0:16:39.31,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,One as first-rate as me doesn't remember \Nanyone beyond the first hundred!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.31,0:16:40.80,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Yeah, I figured!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.80,0:16:44.13,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,So anyway, out of the names I remember...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.13,0:16:46.02,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Let's see... Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.02,0:16:47.02,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,What about Reid?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.02,0:16:50.03,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Was it you who killed\Nthe first Sword Saint?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.28,0:16:52.75,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Hey, watch it!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.44,0:16:57.12,main,Meili,0,0,0,,Th-Thanks, Big Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.12,0:17:00.83,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Nah, it kinda happened because I \Nblurted that out without warning.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.11,0:17:04.59,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,What? Does the first Sword \NSaint scare you that much?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.64,0:17:07.46,main,Julius,0,0,0,,Don't be silly.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.00,0:17:11.48,main,Julius,0,0,0,,He's the progenitor of the Astrea family, \Nincluding Reinhard and his grandfather.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.48,0:17:15.23,main,Julius,0,0,0,,In addition to his sword skills, he must \Nhave been a man of great character.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.23,0:17:18.68,main,Julius,0,0,0,,Miss Shaula, allow us to hear your \Nthoughts without reservation.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.45,0:17:21.39,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,He was human scum.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.26,0:17:26.69,main,Julius,0,0,0,,Allow us to hear your thoughts \Nwithout reservation.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.69,0:17:28.10,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Don't pretend she never said it!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.60,0:17:31.24,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Well, at any rate, he was an awful person.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.24,0:17:34.71,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Like when a rotten little brat \Ngrows up and still doesn't change.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.71,0:17:37.61,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,He absolutely loved bullying the weak.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.03,0:17:42.70,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Hell, from his perspective, pretty \Nmuch everyone was a weakling,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.70,0:17:45.84,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,so no matter who he fought, \Nhe was bullying the weak.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.84,0:17:47.58,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,He did it to me all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.58,0:17:51.29,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,He must've been a real monster \Nif he got the better of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.29,0:17:52.66,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Actually, wait...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.66,0:17:57.44,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,There's a chance that challengers have \Nto defeat Shaula to enter the tower,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.44,0:18:01.12,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,so the answer has to be something \NI'd know without asking her.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.76,0:18:02.87,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,Subaru?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.87,0:18:05.02,main,Anastasia,0,0,0,,Natsuki? Did ya think of somethin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.79,0:18:09.35,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,The possibility of conquering \Nthe tower without Shaula...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.35,0:18:13.96,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,What if there's another Shaula that \NShaula doesn't realize is Shaula?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.94,0:18:17.05,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,What's up, Master?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.05,0:18:20.73,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,You're embarrassing me, \Nstaring at me like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.37,0:18:29.47,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Beako!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.44,0:18:32.59,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,That expression...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.96,0:18:36.17,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,That's the expression \NBetty likes to see on you!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.17,0:18:40.79,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I want to jump up high and look \Nat these monoliths from above.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.89,0:18:45.07,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,Murak!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.54,0:18:52.07,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Just like I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.07,0:18:53.80,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,Did you achieve your goal, I suppose?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.80,0:18:54.48,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I sure did!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.56,0:18:56.73,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,This place...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.32,0:19:00.26,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,is as sadistic as they come.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.54,0:19:08.16,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I know the hero's name.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.70,0:19:09.00,Episode Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&\an8\bord2}A White Sky Asterism
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.80,0:20:43.84,main,Anastasia,0,0,0,,Natsuki, how did ya figure out the answer?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.84,0:20:45.97,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,It wasn't that big a deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.29,0:20:48.93,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,It's not you guys' fault \Nyou couldn't solve it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.26,0:20:52.39,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,There are very few people \Nin this world who could.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.68,0:20:56.76,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,The name of the hero\Nvanquished by Shaula...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.76,0:20:57.81,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,was Orion.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.49,0:20:59.81,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,Orion?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.88,0:21:04.37,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,Wait, wait! I've never heard of any Orion!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.37,0:21:06.50,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I wouldn't expect you to.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.50,0:21:10.49,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,The "Shaula" in the question \Nwasn't even you at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.49,0:21:12.84,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,But I'm the only Shaula!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.84,0:21:14.73,main,Shaula,0,0,0,,That's the name you gave me, Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.73,0:21:19.67,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,I'm saying the name your master \Ngave you has a story behind it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.67,0:21:22.43,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,The story behind Shaula's name?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.43,0:21:25.17,main,Emilia,0,0,0,,Is this another thing that \Nonly you know, Subaru?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.17,0:21:28.07,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Well, not {\i0}only{\i0} me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.07,0:21:31.32,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Where I come from,\Nthere's a star named Shaula.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.32,0:21:36.14,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,It means "stinger," but specifically, \Nit refers to a scorpion's tail.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.47,0:21:38.10,main,Meili,0,0,0,,A scorpion?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.10,0:21:42.91,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Legends say the hero Orion let \Nhis ego get the better of him,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.91,0:21:45.96,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,so he got stung and killed by a \Nscorpion that was sent to torment him,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.96,0:21:47.07,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,and turned into stars.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.59,0:21:51.84,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,And for its achievement, the scorpion \Nwas also turned into a star.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.84,0:21:56.54,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,They say Orion is still terrified of \Nthat scorpion, even up in the night sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.54,0:22:01.01,main,Beatrice,0,0,0,,When you simplify it that much,\Neven a hero's tale sounds disappointing.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.01,0:22:02.13,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Anyway!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.83,0:22:07.32,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Groups of stars that resemble people \Nor animals are known as constellations.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.32,0:22:10.57,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,They can also be called asterisms.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.57,0:22:15.28,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,And when I looked down at the monoliths \Nfrom above... there it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.43,0:22:21.40,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Then, when I envisioned the \Nconstellations and found Orion...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.40,0:22:22.57,main,Julius,0,0,0,,When you found it?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.31,0:22:27.97,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,"His grandest splendor" is a tricky \Nway to phrase the question.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:27.97,0:22:30.56,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,The thing is, different stars \Nshine in different ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.56,0:22:34.58,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,Some are consistently bright,\Nwhile others flash brighter at times.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.26,0:22:39.39,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,There are two stars in Orion that \Ncould be said to shine the brightest.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.94,0:22:42.46,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,There's Rigel,\Nwhich shines consistently...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.87,0:22:46.33,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,and Betelgeuse, a variable star \Nthat glows extra bright at times.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.22,0:22:53.30,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,But it's not very elegant to have \Ntwo acceptable answers, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.47,0:22:59.28,main,Subaru,0,0,0,,If it were me, I think I'd choose Rigel.

